// (the vrx-api ↔ vrx-agent contract, P03/P03b) carries no VPN domain messages yet. The messages are
// written so they can be moved into packages/proto/vrx/v1 verbatim as an additive contract change
// (D-034 style: strings for enums, JSON-compatible, no VPP handles).
//
// Secrets never appear here. Every key/PSK field is a *reference* the descriptor resolves through
// vpn.Resolver at apply time:
//   "sha256:<hex>"          symmetric material (SA keys, IKEv2 PSK, WireGuard preshared key) —
//                           the hex SHA-256 of the material;
//   "x25519:<base64 pub>"   a WireGuard private key, referenced by its public key (std base64).
// Because the reference is derived from the material, Retrieve can rebuild it from what VPP exposes
// (SA keys are returned by ipsec_sa_v5_dump, the PSK by ikev2_profile_dump, the preshared key by
// wireguard_peers_v2_dump, the public key by wireguard_interface_dump) without ever putting the
